mooncakes sync image mirrors the MoonBit mooncakes.io registry.

It syncs both parts of the registry:

1. the Git index from https://mooncakes.io/git/index
2. the package storage bucket from s3://moonbitlang-mooncakes

The default output layout is:

```
/data/
  index/      # bare Git repository for the registry index
  download/   # package storage files
```

The index repository is updated with `git fetch`, repacked, and prepared for
HTTP serving with `git update-server-info`. The package storage is synced with
anonymous rclone S3 access.

For a mirror served as `https://mirrors.example/mooncakes`, users can configure
MoonBit with:

```json
{
  "registry": "https://mirrors.example/mooncakes/download",
  "index": "https://mirrors.example/mooncakes/index",
  "symbols": "https://mirrors.example/mooncakes/download/symbols.zip"
}
```

Then update the registry index and install a package:

```sh
moon update
moon install moonbit-community/warren
```

Useful image options:

- `MOONCAKES_INDEX_URL`: registry index Git URL. Defaults to `https://mooncakes.io/git/index`.
- `MOONCAKES_INDEX_DIR`: directory name for the bare Git index under `/data`. Defaults to `index`.
- `MOONCAKES_DOWNLOAD_DIR`: directory name for package storage under `/data`. Defaults to `download`.
- `MOONCAKES_BUCKET`: S3 bucket name for package storage. Defaults to `moonbitlang-mooncakes`.
- `MOONCAKES_REGION`: S3 bucket region. Defaults to `us-west-2`.
- `MOONCAKES_RCLONE_EXTRA`: extra options passed to `rclone sync`. Defaults to empty.
- `RCLONE_CHECKERS`: number of rclone checkers. Defaults to `$(getconf _NPROCESSORS_ONLN)`.
- `RCLONE_TRANSFERS`: number of rclone transfers. Defaults to `$(getconf _NPROCESSORS_ONLN)`.
